The central type is
\fBeconf\&.File\fR, the in\-memory representation of a parsed and/or merged
configuration\&. Values are read from and written to a
\fI*File\fR
using typed getter/setter methods, mirroring the
\fCeconf_get*Value\fR/\fCeconf_set*Value\fR
family of C functions\&.

.PP
Errors are returned as
\fI*econf\&.Error\fR; callers compare against the sentinel values
(\fCeconf\&.ErrNoKey\fR,
\fCeconf\&.ErrNoGroup\fR, \&.\&.\&.) with
\fBerrors\&.Is\fR(3)\&. See
\fBeconf_go_Error\fR(3)\&.

.SS "Constructors"

.PP
\fBNewKeyFile\fR,
\fBNewKeyFileWithOptions\fR,
\fBNewIniFile\fR
create a new, empty
\fI*File\fR\&. See
\fBeconf_go_NewKeyFile\fR(3)\&.

.SS "Reading"

.PP
\fBReadFile\fR,
\fBReadFileWithCallback\fR
parse a single configuration file\&. See
\fBeconf_go_ReadFile\fR(3)\&.

.PP
\fBReadConfig\fR,
\fBReadConfigWithCallback\fR
evaluate and merge configuration files for a project from the vendor,
runtime and admin directories\&. See
\fBeconf_go_ReadConfig\fR(3)\&.

.PP
\fBReadDirsHistory\fR,
\fBReadDirsHistoryWithCallback\fR
return one
\fI*File\fR
per configuration file found, instead of a single merged result\&. See
\fBeconf_go_ReadDirsHistory\fR(3)\&.

.PP
\fBMergeFiles\fR
merges two already\-parsed
\fI*File\fR
values\&. See
\fBeconf_go_MergeFiles\fR(3)\&.

.SS "Writing"

.PP
\fB(*File)\&.WriteFile\fR
writes a
\fI*File\fR's contents to disk\&. See
\fBeconf_go_File_WriteFile\fR(3)\&.

.SS "Introspection"

.PP
\fB(*File)\&.Path\fR
returns the path a file was parsed from\&. See
\fBeconf_go_File_Path\fR(3)\&.

.PP
\fB(*File)\&.Groups\fR
and
\fB(*File)\&.Keys\fR
list the groups and keys of a file\&. See
\fBeconf_go_File_Groups\fR(3)\&.

.PP
\fB(*File)\&.CommentTag\fR,
\fB(*File)\&.SetCommentTag\fR,
\fB(*File)\&.DelimiterTag\fR
and
\fB(*File)\&.SetDelimiterTag\fR
get/set the comment and delimiter characters of a file\&. See
\fBeconf_go_File_Tags\fR(3)\&.

.PP
\fB(*File)\&.HasQuotes\fR
reports whether a value is enclosed by quotes\&. See
\fBeconf_go_File_HasQuotes\fR(3)\&.

.SS "Getters and setters"

.PP
Typed getters
(\fBInt\fR,
\fBInt64\fR,
\fBUInt\fR,
\fBUInt64\fR,
\fBFloat\fR,
\fBDouble\fR,
\fBString\fR,
\fBBool\fR), each with a
\fB\&.\&.\&.Def\fR
variant taking a default value\&. See
\fBeconf_go_File_Get\fR(3)\&.

.PP
Typed setters
(\fBSetInt\fR,
\fBSetInt64\fR,
\fBSetUInt\fR,
\fBSetUInt64\fR,
\fBSetFloat\fR,
\fBSetDouble\fR,
\fBSetString\fR,
\fBSetBool\fR), plus
\fBSetQuotes\fR\&. See
\fBeconf_go_File_Set\fR(3)\&.

.SS "Cleanup"

.PP
\fB(*File)\&.Close\fR
is a no\-op, provided only for API compatibility with the cgo\-based
binding\&. See
\fBeconf_go_File_Close\fR(3)\&.

.SS "Callbacks"

.PP
\fBFileCallback\fR
is the function type accepted by the
\fB\&.\&.\&.WithCallback\fR
read functions\&. See
\fBeconf_go_FileCallback\fR(3)\&.

.SS "Deliberately not implemented"

.PP
The deprecated
\fCeconf_readDirs\fR/\fCeconf_readDirsWithCallback\fR
functions, the extended
\fCeconf_getExtValue\fR/\fCeconf_setExtValue\fR
API, and the non\-thread\-safe global setters
(\fCeconf_requireOwner\fR,
\fCeconf_requireGroup\fR,
\fCeconf_requirePermissions\fR,
\fCeconf_followSymlinks\fR,
\fCeconf_reset_security_settings\fR,
\fCeconf_set_conf_dirs\fR) \(em matching the cgo\-based binding, which does
not wrap them either\&.

